From: C2000Max local integration
Subject: [PATCH] hwifi: explicitly include the kernel bitfield helpers

Patch 008 already guards the local fallback definitions. Include their
kernel provider explicitly before those guards instead of depending on
transitive inclusion through os/mt_linux.h. This also supports the 6.12
backport of the non-constant lowercase field_prep()/field_get() helpers.

--- a/wlan_hwifi/utility.h
+++ b/wlan_hwifi/utility.h
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 #include "hwifi_muldf.h"
 #endif /* CONFIG_MULDF_HELPER */
 #include "os/mt_linux.h"
+#include <linux/bitfield.h>
 
 #ifndef __bf_shf
 #define __bf_shf(x) (__builtin_ffsll(x) - 1)
